  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "wrIhv8StaMWfNVr9VUT4lEHn6bw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:16.621Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`SyncStatus` is not a field the reactor writes and updates. It is **computed on demand from the depth of the channel's mailboxes**, which is why it can never drift out of step with the actual queues.\n\n```typescript\ngetSyncStatus(documentId: string): SyncStatus | undefined;\nonSyncStatusChange(callback: SyncStatusChangeCallback): () => void;\n```\n\n```typescript\nenum SyncStatus {\n  Synced = \"SYNCED\",\n  Outgoing = \"OUTGOING\",\n  Incoming = \"INCOMING\",\n  OutgoingAndIncoming = \"OUTGOING_AND_INCOMING\",\n  Error = \"ERROR\",\n}\n```\n\nThe derivation rules are strictly ordered: **any error gives `Error`**; pending work in both directions gives `OutgoingAndIncoming`; otherwise it is `Incoming`, `Outgoing`, or \u2014 with both mailboxes empty \u2014 `Synced`. Because error wins, `Error` does not tell you the direction failed in; read the dead-letter events or the per-remote connection state for that.\n\n`getSyncStatus` returns `undefined` for a document that has never been tracked. That is a distinct third state from \"synced\" and worth handling explicitly in UI: absent, not clean. `onSyncStatusChange` returns an unsubscribe function, and its callback is `(documentId: string, status: SyncStatus) => void`.\n\nThis per-document view is one of three. The other two are per-job (`waitForSync(jobId)`, which resolves \u2014 never rejects \u2014 on both success and failure, carrying `status: \"succeeded\" | \"failed\"`) and per-remote (`channel.getConnectionState()`, returning a `ConnectionStateSnapshot` with `state`, `failureCount`, `pushBlocked`, `receivingPages`, and `requiresAuth`).\n\nThere is a hard boundary to be aware of: when the sync manager runs in a SharedWorker and you hold the tab-side RPC proxy, `waitForSync` **always** rejects with `\"waitForSync is not supported over the worker RPC boundary\"`. In that topology the mailbox-derived `getSyncStatus` / `onSyncStatusChange` pair and per-remote connection state are your only observability, which makes this derived status the more portable of the three views.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/04-Synchronization.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:34:15.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:16.621Z"
    }
  },
